Backport of arvidn/libtorrent e7049d21d33583eb2b0d672b07468aefd26805ec
("fix dh shared secret padding", RC_2_0, 2026-05-31; also in v2.1.0).

compute_secret() hashed the req3 xor mask over a 96-byte buffer that
mp::export_bits() only partly fills when the DH shared secret has a leading
zero byte (~1/256 handshakes): the tail stays uninitialized, the two ends
derive different masks, and the receiving side rejects the MSE handshake
with "invalid info-hash" right after finding the sync hash. export_key()
pads to 96 bytes exactly like the req1 sync hash and the RC4 keys already do.

--- a/src/pe_crypto.cpp
+++ b/src/pe_crypto.cpp
@@ -117,8 +117,7 @@
 		// shared_secret = (remote_pubkey ^ local_secret) % prime
 		m_dh_shared_secret = mp::powm(remote_pubkey, m_dh_local_secret, dh_prime);
 
-		std::array<char, 96> buffer;
-		mp::export_bits(m_dh_shared_secret, reinterpret_cast<std::uint8_t*>(buffer.data()), 8);
+		std::array<char, 96> const buffer = export_key(m_dh_shared_secret);
 
 		static char const req3[4] = {'r', 'e', 'q', '3'};
 		// calculate the xor mask for the obfuscated hash
